                ],
                'urdu_body' => "Mutual Funds aam Pakistani retail investor ke liye market mein dakhil hone ka sab se aasaan aur safe tareeqa hai.\n\nIs mein aap ko khud companies ki balance sheets check karne ki zaroorat nahi hoti, balkay professional Fund Managers (jaise Al Meezan, UBL Funds, MCB Funds) aap ka paisa mukhtalif stocks ya government T-Bills mein invest kartay hain.\n\nAgar aap safe monthly munafa chahtay hain to Money Market / Income Funds behtareen hain. Agar aap 5-10 saal ke liye daulat barhana chahtay hain to Equity Funds behtar hain.",
                'body' => "Mutual funds represent the most accessible entry point for everyday Pakistani salaried professionals, freelancers, and students wanting to beat inflation without managing individual stocks.\n\n### How Mutual Funds Work in Pakistan\nWhen you invest in an Asset Management Company (AMC) regulated by the Securities & Exchange Commission of Pakistan (SECP), your capital is pooled with other retail and institutional investors. A professional team of CFA charterholders and financial analysts manages the allocation.\n\n### The Major Fund Categories:\n1. **Money Market Funds (Low Risk)**: Invests in 3-month to 6-month Government Treasury Bills (T-Bills) and high-grade bank deposits. Great for emergency funds.\n2. **Income Funds (Low-to-Moderate Risk)**: Invests in government Pakistan Investment Bonds (PIBs) and corporate Sukuks for competitive regular yields.\n3. **Equity Funds (Moderate-to-High Risk)**: Invests directly in PSX KSE-100 listed equities like Meezan Bank, Hubco, and Lucky Cement. Built for long-term wealth creation (3–7 years).",
            ],
            [
                'title' => 'CDC Sub-Account vs Investor Account (IAS): Which One Do You Need?',
