                    'question' => 'What is the primary security advantage of holding long-term shares in a direct CDC Investor Account (IAS)?',
                    'options' => ['SECP pays you 20% annual guaranteed bonus', 'Shares are held directly in your name with CDC and cannot be moved or pledged by a broker', 'You never pay any brokerage commissions', 'Automatic exemption from dividend tax'],
                    'correct_index' => 1,
                    'explanation' => 'Direct CDC Investor Accounts ring-fence custody directly with the central depository, safeguarding your equity ownership even if a brokerage firm faces insolvency.',
                ],
                'urdu_body' => "PSX par shares khareednay ke baad aap ke shares physical certificates mein nahi, balkay electronic shakal mein Central Depository Company (CDC) ke paas mehfooz hotay hain.\n\nSub-Account: Yeh aap ka broker aap ke liye CDC system ke andar banata hai. Is ke zariye rozana buy/sell orders fast execute hotay hain.\n\nInvestor Account (IAS): Yeh direct CDC ke sath aap ka zati safe-deposit box hota hai. Broker is mein se aap ke shares ko aap ke direct SMS/Biometric authorization ke baghair hath nahi laga sakta. Long-term wealth ke liye IAS behtareen protection hai.",
                'body' => "Whenever you purchase shares of a Pakistani company like Meezan Bank (\$MEBL) or Oil & Gas Development Co (\$OGDC), you don't receive paper certificates. Instead, the Central Depository Company of Pakistan (CDC) records your ownership electronically.\n\n### The Two Types of Custody Accounts:\n\n#### 1. Broker Sub-Account\nWhen you open an online trading account with a licensed PSX broker (e.g., AKD, Arif Habib, JS Global), a sub-account is created under the broker's umbrella participant account. It is fast, convenient, and enables instantaneous electronic settlement through NCCPL.\n\n#### 2. CDC Investor Account (IAS)\nAn Investor Account is opened directly with CDC Pakistan (independent of any broker). Shares parked in your IAS cannot be pledged, transferred, or manipulated by any third party without your explicit direct authorization.\n\n### Recommended Best Practice:\nKeep your active trading capital in your broker sub-account. Once you build a substantial core position in dividend aristocrats that you plan to hold for 5+ years, transfer those shares to your CDC Investor Account for maximum structural safety.",
