                'quiz_data' => [
                    'question' => 'Why can the KSE-100 index close up +600 points even when 60% of all listed companies closed in the red?',
                    'options' => ['SECP manually overrides index points on Mondays', 'The KSE-100 is market-cap weighted, meaning top companies like MCB, FFC, and OGDC have significantly more influence on the points than smaller companies', 'Only foreign institutions are counted in the points calculation', 'Mutual funds reset their balances every evening'],
                    'correct_index' => 1,
                    'explanation' => 'Because the KSE-100 is market-cap weighted, rallies in large-cap heavyweights (like banking and fertilizer giants) contribute more points than dozens of smaller companies falling.',
                ],
                'urdu_body' => "KSE-100 index Pakistan Stock Exchange ka markazi barometer hai. Jab aap news mein suntay hain ke 'PSX 1,000 points barh gayi', to is ka matlab KSE-100 index mein izafa hua hai.\n\nIndex mein har sector ki top company aur market cap ke lehaaz se sab se bari 100 companies shamil hoti hain.\n\nSab se ahem baat: 3 baray sectors (Banks, Fertilizer, aur Oil & Gas) pooray index ka 50% se zyada hissa hain. Agar banks aur fertilizer barh rahay hon to baqi choti companies girnay ke bawajood index green nazar aata hai.",
                'body' => "Every business headline in Pakistan reports the daily point change of the KSE-100 index. But what does that number actually measure?\n\n### Composition of the KSE-100\nThe KSE-100 was introduced in November 1991 with a base value of 1,000 points. Today, it reflects approximately 85% of the total market capitalization of all companies listed on the PSX.\n\nThe 100 companies are selected according to strict rules:\n- **Sector Leaders**: The company with the highest market capitalization from each of the 36 sectors is automatically inducted.\n- **Market Cap Ranking**: The remaining 64 spots are filled by the largest companies regardless of sector.\n\n### Understanding Sector Heavyweights\nBecause the index is market-capitalization weighted, not all 100 stocks carry equal weight. In fact, three sectors dictate more than half of the daily point swings:\n1. **Commercial Banks** (MCB, UBL, MEBL, HBL)\n2. **Fertilizer** (FFC, ENGRO, EFERT)\n3. **Oil & Gas Exploration** (OGDC, PPL, MARI)\n\nUnderstanding this dynamic prevents panic: when headlines scream about a 1,000-point fall, savvy retail investors check whether the drop was concentrated in a single sector due to a tax policy change or if the broader market remains fundamentally strong.",
            ],
