                ],
                'urdu_body' => "Pakistan Stock Exchange mein Islamic investments ke liye KMI-30 (KSE Meezan Index) banaya gaya hai.\n\nShariah Board 6 sakht usoolon ke tehat har 6 maah baad companies ki screening karta hai:\n1. Business Halal hona chahiye (Conventional Banks, Casino, Sharab shamil nahi).\n2. Interest-bearing qarza Total Assets ke 37% se kam hona chahiye.\n3. Haram zariya se aane wali aamdani (agar koi ho) ko Dividend Purification ke zariye charity mein dena zaroori hota hai.\n\nIs screening ki madad se aap ba-aasani Meezan Bank, Lucky Cement, Engro Corporation, aur Systems Limited jaisi Shariah-compliant companies mein invest kar saktay hain.",
                'body' => "For millions of Pakistani Muslims, participating in capital markets requires strict adherence to Islamic financial principles. The KSE-Meezan Index (KMI-30) was co-developed by Al-Meezan Investment Management and the PSX to track the performance of top Shariah-compliant equities.\n\n### The 6-Point Shariah Screening Framework\nA company must satisfy all six criteria established by reputable Shariah scholars and approved by the SECP:\n\n1. **Core Business Activity**: The core business must be permissible. Conventional interest-based commercial banks, life insurance providers, and gambling enterprises are categorically excluded.\n2. **Interest-Bearing Debt to Total Assets**: Total interest-bearing debt must be **less than 37%** of total assets.\n3. **Non-Compliant Investments to Total Assets**: Investments in conventional interest-bearing deposits, T-Bills, or bonds must be **less than 33%** of total assets.\n4. **Non-Compliant Income to Total Revenue**: Any incidental interest income earned on operational bank accounts must not exceed **5%** of total gross revenue.\n5. **Illiquid Assets to Total Assets**: At least **25%** of total assets must be tangible, illiquid assets (plant, machinery, inventory), ensuring the share represents an actual business interest rather than just currency trading.\n6. **Market Price vs Net Liquid Assets**: Market price per share must exceed net liquid assets per share.\n\n### Dividend Purification\nIf a Shariah-compliant firm earns 1% of its revenue from temporary cash parked in an interest-bearing account, Shariah guidelines require the investor to 'purify' their dividends by donating that exact 1% proportion to charity.",
